## What to Do With What You Find

| Finding                   | Immediate Next Action                         |
| ------------------------- | --------------------------------------------- |
| Usernames                 | Add to users list → password spraying         |
| Email addresses           | Domain confirmed, possible phishing/OSINT     |
| AV process names          | Know what you're up against before exploiting |
| Vulnerable software + ver | `searchsploit <name> <version>`               |
| Internal TCP ports        | Enumerate those services (may need tunneling) |
| Hostname / domain name    | Confirms AD target, feeds DNS enumeration     |
| Private community string  | Attempt TFTP config pull on network hardware  |

---

## Gotchas & Exam Tips

* **Always run UDP scans.** TCP-only recon misses SNMP entirely.
* If `-v1` returns nothing, retry with `-v2c`.
* The `-t 10` timeout matters heavily over VPNs and slow networks.
* Cross-reference running processes with installed software versions.
* SNMP on routers/switches with the `private` string can become catastrophic.
* Document every username you discover.

